[23.271145, "o", "bash /opt/gnomon-run.sh 'There'\"'\"'s something wrong with my system-wide python installation - I can'\"'\"'t seem to install packages with pip.'; tmux wait -S done\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[70.395737, "o", "`ensurepip` trusts the leftover `dist-info` and concludes pip is fine. The stale metadata has to be cleared before it will reinstall from the bundled wheel.\r\n\r\n## The fix\r\n\r\nThe offline wheel `ensurepip/_bundled/pip-24.3.1-py3-none-any.whl` was intact, so no network was needed:\r\n\r\n1. Backed up the broken metadata to `/tmp/piptriage/`.\r\n2. Removed `site-packages/pip-24.3.1.dist-info` and the orphaned `/usr/local/bin/pip3.13`.\r\n3. `python3 -m ensurepip --default-pip` → reinstalled pip 24.3.1 from the local wheel.\r\n\r\n## Verification\r\n\r\n`/tmp/verify_pip.sh` — I wrote it to fail if any of this regresses, and it passes end to end:\r\n\r\n```\r\nPASS  python3 -m pip --version\r\nPASS  pip --version (bare)\r\nPASS  pip3 --version\r\nPASS  import pip\r\nPASS  pip.__version__ == 24.3.1\r\nPASS  pip submodules importable\r\nPASS  site-packages/pip exists\r\nPASS  no stale/missing-file state\r\nPASS  pip list runs\r\nPASS  pip can resolve a real install\r\nPASS  file count matches RECORD (841)\r\n---\r\nALL CHECKS PASSED\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe last check is"]
[70.395921, "o", " the one that matters most for your symptom: I did a genuine `pip install six` in a throwaway venv (`Successfully installed six-1.17.0`, then `import six` → `1.17.0`), and a `--dry-run` install against the network. Both work. `pip check` reports `No broken requirements found.`\r\n\r\n## Two things worth noting\r\n\r\n- **This was damage, not misconfiguration.** The directory was deleted at some point (note the site-packages mtime of Oct 31 vs the package files' Jan 14) — likely a manual `rm`, or an interrupted/interleaved install. It'll recur if whatever deleted it runs again; check any cleanup or image-pruning scripts that touch `site-packages`.\r\n- **pip 24.3.1 is behind** (26.2.2 is current). I deliberately left it — you asked me to fix a broken install, not to change your package versions. `python3 -m pip install --upgrade pip` when you want it.\r\n\r\nBackup of the broken metadata is at `/tmp/piptriage/` if you want to inspect it; delete it whenever. The script is at `/tmp/verify_pip.sh`.\r\n\r\n[result] role=imple"]
